{"1421":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">APTITUDE: NUMBERS, PERCENT, SPEED &amp; SETS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.19em;font-weight:700\">EXPONENTS · LCM · DIGITS · % &amp; PROFIT · SPEED, TRAINS, BOATS, WORK · VENN — PAST GA SUMS</p><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.19em;font-weight:700\">(CHECKED)</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Numbers</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Idea</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Rule</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Past-paper example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Exponent laws</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">aᵐ·aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ · aᵐ/aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ · (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ · a⁰ = 1 · a<sup>1/n</sup> = ⁿ√a</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">write numbers as prime powers: 27 = 3³, 162 = 2·3⁴</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Perfect square / cube</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">every prime exponent even / a multiple of 3</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">162 = 2·3⁴ → × 2²·3² = 36 gives 18³</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Number of digits</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">⌊log₁₀N⌋ + 1</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">(4.7×10²⁹)³ ≈ 1.04×10⁸⁹ → 90 digits</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">LCM &amp; HCF</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">LCM × HCF = product of two numbers; events repeat together after the LCM</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">every 20, 30, 50 min → together after 300 min</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Divisibility</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">3, 9: digit sum · 4: last two digits · 8: last three · 11: alternate-digit difference</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">—</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Unit digit</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">2, 3, 7, 8 repeat every 4 powers; 0, 1, 5, 6 fixed; 4, 9 every 2</td><td data-h=\"Past-paper example\">3⁹⁹⁹·7¹⁰⁰⁰ → 7 × 1 = 7</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Percent, profit, average</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Idea</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Rule</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">% change</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">(new − old)/old × 100</td><td data-h=\"Example\">old 40 → new 50: +25 %</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Successive changes</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">(1 + a)(1 + b) − 1 = a + b + ab</td><td data-h=\"Example\">+10 % then −10 % → −1 %</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Profit / loss</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">profit % = (SP − CP)/CP × 100</td><td data-h=\"Example\">CP 1700, SP 1800 → 5 15/17 %</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Discount, tax</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">SP = MP(1 − d); price with tax = SP(1 + t)</td><td data-h=\"Example\">work back by dividing: 3186/1.18/1.20 = 2250</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Weighted average</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">Σwᵢxᵢ / Σwᵢ</td><td data-h=\"Example\">boys 4/7, girls 3/7 of candidates</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Ratio</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">x : y = a : b → x = ak, y = bk</td><td data-h=\"Example\">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fef8f4;border-color:#ef6c00\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#ef6c00\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#ef6c00;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#ef6c00;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Speed, time &amp; work</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Idea</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Rule</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Distance</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">d = v·t; km/h × 5/18 = m/s</td><td data-h=\"Example\">45 km/h = 12.5 m/s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Relative speed</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">same direction v₁ − v₂, opposite v₁ + v₂</td><td data-h=\"Example\">—</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Train crossing</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">train length (+ platform/bridge length) = v·t</td><td data-h=\"Example\">12.5 × 30 − 130 = 245 m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Boats &amp; streams</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">down = u + v, up = u − v → u = (down + up)/2, v = (down − up)/2</td><td data-h=\"Example\">up 2, down 6 → still water 4 km/h</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Work &amp; pipes</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">rates add: 1/T = 1/T₁ + 1/T₂; emptying pipe subtracts</td><td data-h=\"Example\">2 h and 4 h together → 4/3 h = 80 min</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Clock &amp; calendar</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">angle |30H − 5.5M|; hands meet every 65 5/11 min; leap year = 2 odd days</td><td data-h=\"Example\">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f8f5fa;border-color:#6a1b9a\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#6a1b9a\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#6a1b9a;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#6a1b9a;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Sets &amp; Venn diagrams</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Idea</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Rule</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Two sets</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">n(A ∪ B) = n(A) + n(B) − n(A ∩ B); neither = total − n(A ∪ B)</td><td data-h=\"Example\">25 − (15 + 17 − 10) = 3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Three sets</td><td data-h=\"Rule\">n(A∪B∪C) = ΣA − Σ(two at a time) + n(A∩B∩C)</td><td data-h=\"Example\">draw the Venn and fill from the centre out</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",[]],"1422":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">CALCULUS BY PICTURE</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-weight:700\">DERIVATIVE CIRCLE · INTEGRAL = AREA UNDER THE GRAPH</p><i data-k=\"6\"></i><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f7f3ff;border-color:#b39ddb\"><i data-k=\"0\"></i><i data-k=\"1\"></i><i data-k=\"2\"></i><i data-k=\"3\"></i><i data-k=\"4\"></i><i data-k=\"5\"></i></div><p><b>Area trick:</b> when the graph is a rectangle, triangle or part of a circle, the definite integral is just that area. Area below the x-axis counts as negative, so odd functions over −a to a give 0.</p>",[["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,0,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,474,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,948,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,1422,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,1896,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,2370,406,468,224],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,2844,901,421,707]]],"1423":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">CALCULUS BY PICTURE (2)</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.19em;font-weight:700\">MAXIMA &amp; MINIMA · ROLLE · MEAN VALUE · CONVEX · TWO-VARIABLE TEST</p><i data-k=\"0\"></i><i data-k=\"1\"></i><i data-k=\"2\"></i><i data-k=\"3\"></i><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f7f7;border-color:#37474f\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#37474f\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#37474f;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#37474f;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Two-variable maxima / minima (13 GATE questions)</p></div><p style=\"font-size:1.10em\"><b>Two variables f(x, y):</b> solve f<sub>x</sub> = 0 and f<sub>y</sub> = 0 → stationary points. Then r = f<sub>xx</sub>, s = f<sub>xy</sub>, t = f<sub>yy</sub>.</p><p style=\"font-size:1.10em\"><b>rt − s² &gt; 0</b> and r &lt; 0 → maximum · rt − s² &gt; 0 and r &gt; 0 → minimum · <b>rt − s² &lt; 0</b> → saddle point (up one way, down the other) · rt − s² = 0 → test fails, look further.</p><p style=\"font-size:1.10em\"><b>Example:</b> f = x² + y² − 4x → f<sub>x</sub> = 2x − 4 = 0, f<sub>y</sub> = 2y = 0 → (2, 0); r = 2, s = 0, t = 2 → rt − s² = 4 &gt; 0, r &gt; 0 → minimum f = −4.</p></div>",[["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,3271,672,494,371],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,3771,672,494,371],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,4271,672,494,371],["img/refp/aptitude-0.webp",901,5265,4771,672,494,371]]],"1424":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">ALGEBRAIC IDENTITIES — SHORTCUT TRICKS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-weight:700\">REMEMBER THE LADDER · ANSWER IN ONE LINE</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fcf5f8;border-color:#c2185b\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#c2185b\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#c2185b;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;background:#c2185b;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">IF  x + 1/x = a</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c2185b\">1.</span> x + 1/x = a</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">given</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c2185b\">2.</span> x² + 1/x² = a² − 2</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">a = 3 → 7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c2185b\">3.</span> x³ + 1/x³ = a³ − 3a</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">a = 3 → 18</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c2185b\">4.</span> x⁴ + 1/x⁴ = (a² − 2)² − 2</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">a = 3 → 47</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c2185b\">5.</span> (x − 1/x)² = a² − 4</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">a = 3 → 5</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">IF  x − 1/x = b</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">1.</span> x − 1/x = b</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">given</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">2.</span> x² + 1/x² = b² + 2</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">b = 2 → 6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">3.</span> x³ − 1/x³ = b³ + 3b</td><td style=\"color:#c62828;font-weight:700\">b = 2 → 14</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fef8f4;border-color:#ef6c00\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#ef6c00\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#ef6c00;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;background:#ef6c00;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Standard Identities</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">(a + b)²</td><td>= a² + 2ab + b²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">(a − b)²</td><td>= a² − 2ab + b²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">a² − b²</td><td>= (a + b)(a − b)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">(a + b)³</td><td>= a³ + b³ + 3ab(a + b)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">(a − b)³</td><td>= a³ − b³ − 3ab(a − b)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">a³ + b³</td><td>= (a + b)(a² − ab + b²)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">a³ − b³</td><td>= (a − b)(a² + ab + b²)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">a³ + b³ + c³ − 3abc</td><td>= (a + b + c)(a² + b² + c² − ab − bc − ca)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">if a + b + c = 0</td><td>= a³ + b³ + c³ = 3abc</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Fast Arithmetic With Identities</p></div><p><b>51 × 49</b> = 50² − 1² = <b>2499</b> (a² − b²)</p><p><b>103²</b> = 100² + 2·100·3 + 3² = <b>10609</b> ((a + b)²)</p><p><b>98²</b> = 100² − 2·100·2 + 2² = <b>9604</b> ((a − b)²)</p><p><b>35²</b>: 3 × 4 = 12, then 25 → <b>1225</b> (squares ending in 5)</p></div>",[]]}